A||N||7||sdelgado||TPS and code 24 question?||||1||
Z||000000||sdelgado||09-29-2001||12:13 PM||||I have an 86 2m4 and I accidentally broke the TPS attach to the TBI.  I replaced it with one from an 84 SE.  Are these swappable or are they different part #???<P>Also, I am getting a code 24, I am not sure if it was after I broke the TPS.  If not, what is the next thing to check, the EGR and baccum hoses?<P>thanks <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||samoht||09-29-2001||06:40 PM||||call NAPA to see if they are interchangable, they will know.. as for the code 24.. a bad TPS can make a code 24.... Does the car ever stall when coming off the interstate or to a stop sign ?  if so I would check the conections to the Speed sensors or replace it if the TPS checks out ok.. Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||samoht||09-29-2001||06:50 PM||||a few more notes about TPS.. the pointy end to the base cant be more than 1 1/4in out (i think) or you can ruin your throttle body by screwing it in to tight, also everytime you replace a TPS it should get a new plastic washer, the is a specail washer that smashes to make a perfect clearance , so even though the sensors look the same they may have had differant spacers,,, I think I would have tried to put the whole throttle body on, instead so swapping TPS.. hope this helps.. beside I think they are really cheap at autozone||||reg||1
Z||000003||samoht||09-29-2001||06:54 PM||||sorry I was thinking ICV.. forget that 2nd reply||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdelgado||09-29-2001||07:32 PM||||thanks for the info samoht.  <P>I actually went down to Pepboys and the TPS is the same for 84 and 86 so I guess I'm ok with that. My idle still jumps around, slightly, from time to time.<P>I also just noticed my speedo wasn't working and when I took the VSS out to check/replace it, noticed that my oil level was way low.  It must be the VSS is bad.  I will have to buy some 5w30 oil tomorrow before I can do more testing.  <P>Could low oil level make the VSS go bad?||||reg||14
Z||000005||Rodrv6||09-29-2001||09:00 PM||||The speedometer problem is likely the cause of your code 24.  The ecm will set a 24 if it doesn't see a speed signal under certain other conditions.  When you took the VSS out, was the plastic gear still attatched to it?  If not, it may have split and fallen into the transaxle.  Low oil shouldn't make the VSS itself go bad, but stranger things have happened.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000006||sdelgado||09-30-2001||02:26 PM||||Well, I took the sensor out and the gear still there.  I will replace the sensor from an used one I have, top the oil and reset the codes.  <P>Oil is somewhat dark, I will like to replace the oil with one of those I've heard in the forum (redline mtl, mobil 1 synthetic, etc), but first I will make sure that code goes away. <P>I will post my results. Thanks.||||reg||7
Z||000007||sdelgado||10-01-2001||11:42 PM||||Well, it looks like the code 24 light went away, but there is still one little problem, the speedometer still does not work!   I'll have to take the speed sensor out and make sure the gear didn't brake, but, that should give me a code 24???  Now I'm really confused!!<P>The idle still jumps from time to time from 1000 to 1500.  I will check for vacuum leaks||||reg||9
